  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 506.04 Start-Up Procedures and Certification Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 506.04 Start-Up Procedures and Certification Required.\n\n(a) Prior to serving water to the public, the owner of a seasonal system shall:\n\n(1) Complete the start-up procedures specified in Env-Dw 506.05; and\n\n(2) Certify to the department that the procedures were completed as specified in Env-Dw 506.06.\n\n(b) The owner may authorize an agent to conduct the start-up procedures and file the certification, but such authorization shall not relieve the owner from liability if the procedures are not done as and when required.\n\nSource. #10771, eff 2-1-15; ss by #14342, eff 8-22-25, EXPIRES: 8-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html"
